---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Abolitionist Fellowship Conference & Mission (2026)"
  description="A recap of the Heritage Restored Abolitionist Fellowship Conference, held January 24, 2026 in Columbus, Ohio — fellowship, preaching, prayer, and street evangelism at WinterJam."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Abolitionist Fellowship Conference &amp; Mission</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This event has already taken place. It was held on Saturday, January 24, 2026.
      If you would like to hear about future gatherings, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Heritage Restored hosted our Abolitionist Fellowship Conference on January 24, 2026 so we could
      have a ton of fellowship, hear from the Word, pray, and encourage one another in the work of abolition.
      Over half the conference time was fellowship, and we had lots of giveaways for those who attended.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>When &amp; Where</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Date:</strong> Saturday, January 24, 2026 |
        <strong>Time:</strong> 11:00 AM &ndash; 3:00 PM <br />
        <strong>What:</strong> Fellowship Conference<br />
        <strong>Location:</strong> The Village Church, 3750 Sullivant Ave, Columbus, OH 43228<br />
        <strong>Cost to attend:</strong> FREE<br />
        <strong>Mission:</strong> Street evangelism at WinterJam, 4&ndash;6 PM
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Conference Schedule (11:00 AM &ndash; 3:00 PM)</h2>

      <div class="schedule-grid">
        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>10:30 AM &ndash; 11:00 AM</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Arrival, Setup, &amp; Check-In</strong>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>11:00 AM &ndash; 12:00 PM | Opening Session</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>11:00 | Welcome &amp; Introductions</strong><br />
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Session 1 - Logan Ramsey</strong><br />
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Session 2 - Elijah Thompson</strong><br />
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>12:00 PM &ndash; 1:00 PM | Lunch &amp; Fellowship</h3>
         </div>

        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>1:00 PM &ndash; 2:00 PM | Mission Preparation Session</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Session 3 - Michael Coughlin</strong><br />
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mission Preparation &amp; Prayer</strong>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>2:00 PM &ndash; 3:00 PM | Fellowship &amp; Clean-Up</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Continued fellowship</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Venue clean-up and closing conversations</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="schedule-block">
          <h3>3:00 PM Depart for Mission to WinterJam</h3>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Speakers</h2>
      <div class="people-grid conference-speakers">
        <div class="person-card">
          <div class="person-photo">
            <img src="/loganramsey.jpg" alt="Pastor Logan J. Ramsey" width="165" height="165" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <h2>Session 1</h2>
          <p><strong>Pastor Logan J. Ramsey</strong></p>
          <p class="person-bio">
            <strong>"The Power for Change"</strong><br />
            Romans 1:16 - God's sovereign grace in salvation means that when we are
            regenerated, our lives are changed on earth. That transformation necessarily leads to faithful work,
            including abolition.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="person-card">
          <div class="person-photo">
            <img src="/elijahthompson.jpg" alt="Elijah Thompson" width="165" height="165" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <h2>Session 2</h2>
          <p><strong>Elijah Thompson</strong></p>
          <p class="person-bio">
            <strong>"Tent-Making Abolitionists"</strong><br />
            How to effectively work for abolition while not being able to dedicate yourself to full-time ministry.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="person-card">
          <div class="person-photo">
            <img src="/michaelcoughlin.jpg" alt="Michael Coughlin" width="165" height="165" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <h2>Session 3</h2>
          <p><strong>Michael Coughlin</strong></p>
          <p class="person-bio">
            <strong>"Loving H8Rs"</strong><br />
            How to respond biblically and effectively to those who oppose you. Defend the voiceless without compromising your personal holiness.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Mission at WinterJam</h2>
      <p>
        After the conference, those still in Columbus met outside the Schottenstein Center for street
        ministry and conversational outreach during WinterJam. Attendees were welcome to come only for the
        mission, only for the fellowship, or for both.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Future Gatherings</h2>
      <p>
        Heritage Restored loves to hear how Christ is working through this ministry. If you would like to be
        told about the next conference and mission, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>. If you would like to help
        underwrite the cost of future gatherings, you can give via our <a href="/donate">donation page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <p class="back-to-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>
